I hope pudding farming _doesn't get eliminated, even
though I've only ever bothered with it myself twice,
so far, being by nature an impatient person. 

Stuff that takes incredible patience to accomplish
isn't "abuse". It is "an alternate playing style".

For those who think ascending, for them, takes
extremes of armor class and equipage and hit points
and skill slots filled, let them spend the time to
acquire them.

For those who think their ascensions should be lean
and mean, using every trick in the book (and some
not yet documented, heh) to ascend in under 20,000
turns, that's okay too.

But the two sides shouldn't be accusing each other
of "abuse".

Those alternative approaches, call them "the walking
tank" and "the walker between raindrops", are just
"style", just like conducts are "just style",

Nor would NetHack be much fun if the Dev Team
decided to eliminate all but _the_ Politically
Correct NetHack Playing Style as "abuses".

Half the fun of the game is figuring out some
_really_ new (or new-to-you) approach to improving
your survival and ascension chances. Having the Dev
Team stamp them out as fast as they are discovered
is rather despiriting.

xanthian.

I still miss the "corner kick" approach to robbing
shops. Figuring that one out for oneself was a pure
exercise in deductive logic from information slowly
gathered by long game experience.

It's loss when "everyone found out" the easy way via
spoilers instead and it became "standard playing
style" is one real example of the tragic dark side
of spoilers.

It's loss as something for the unspoiled player to
invent is just _so_ completely unfair, and is _such_
a loss to the richness of NetHack, a total cave-in
catering to the bad habits of the voluntarily
spoiled..

